(  234) ! NRADIP : INTEGER : INDEX FOR DIAGNOSIS OF ICE CLOUD EFFECTIVE RADIUS
(  235) !          0 = fixed at 40 microns
(  236) !          1 = Liou & Ou (1994) capped between 40-130 microns
(  237) !          2 = Liou & Ou but capped between 30 and 60 microns
(  238) !          3 = Sun & Rikus (1999) revised by Sun (2001)
(  239) ! NRADLP : INTEGER : INDEX FOR DIAGNOSIS OF LIQ. CLOUD EFFECTIVE RADIUS
(  240) !          0 = ERA-15 function of pressure
(  241) !          1 = 10 microns over land, 13 microns over sea
(  242) !          2 = Martin_et_al (1994) in terms of land-sea number conc
(  243) !          3 = Linked to prognostic aerosols
(  244) !          4 = CAMS cloud droplets and ICE3 gamma laws for cloud droplet size distribution are used
(  245) ! NICEOPT: INTEGER : INDEX FOR ICE CLOUD OPTICAL PROPERTIES
(  246) !          0 = SW Ebert-Curry, LW Smith & Shi (1992)
(  247) !          1 = SW Ebert-Curry, LW Ebert-Curry (1992)
(  248) !          2 = SW & LW Fu-Liou (1993)
(  249) !          3 = SW Fu (1996) LW Fu et al. (1998) + Chou et al. (1999) LW scatt approx
(  250) !   the following only available in newer modular radiation scheme:
(  251) !          4 = SW/LW Baran data fitted versus ice mixing ratio
(  252) ! NLIQOPT: INTEGER : INDEX FOR LIQUID WATER CLOUD OPTICAL PROPERTIES
(  253) !          0 = SW Fouquart (1991) LW Smith-Shi (1992) YF/SmSh 
(  254) !          1 = SW Slingo (1989) LW Savijarvi (1997)
(  255) !          2 = SW Slingo (1989) LW Lindner-Li (2000)
(  256) !   the following only available in RADLSW, not RADLSWR:
(  257) !          3 = SW Nielsen       LW Smith-Shi
(  258) !   the following only available in newer modular radiation scheme:
(  259) !          4 = SW/LW SOCRATES scheme
(  260) !
(  261) ! LONEWSW: LOGICAL : .T. IF NEW SW CODE IS ACTIVE
